      "message": "Sorry I didn\u0027t jump in earlier, the 0x3fff that was here before wasn\u0027t actually based on CONFIG_USB_RAM_SIZE, it is a mask on a hardware register that is always defined to have 10 bits.  So either 0x3fff, or a define for that register would make more sense.  The register is a little weird though, since it is actually part of a table stored in the USB packet ram, and not directly accessible via the peripheral bus...",
